Helps you launch 3rd party high performance system on AWS as a full managed service.
for Windows: supports smb protocol& windows NTFS,DFS/distributed file system AD integration,ACLs,user quotas. And can be mounted on linux ec instances
for lustre: type of distributed file system, for large-scale computing, combination of linux and clust. Used for HPC/ High performance computing and seamless integration with s3.
scratch file system: temp storage and data not replicated
persisten file system: long storage, data is replicated withing AZ automatically
for netApp ontap:move workloads running on ontap or nas to aws, autoscaling, snapshots, point-in-time cloning
openzfs: managed openzfs file system on aws, move workload running on zfs to aws, point in time instantaneous cloning


